//! The `max-block-size` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property specifies
//! the maximum size of an element in the direction opposite that of the writing direction as
//! specified by `writing-mode`. That is, if the writing direction is horizontal, then
//! `max-block-size` is equivalent to `max-height`; if the writing direction is vertical,
//! `max-block-size` is the same as `max-width`.
//!
//! Initial: none. Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: block-size of containing block.
//!
//! Grammar: none | <box-size> | <anchor-size()>
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-sizing-3/#propdef-max-block-size
//!
//! Author guide:
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/max-block-size
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

